<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wartislaw III, Duke of Pomerania</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1210–<a href="/years/1264">1264</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wartislaw III was duke of Pomerania-Demmin, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-griffins">Griffin dynasty</a>, ruling alongside his cousin Barnim I. He promoted German settlement and granted town rights, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lubeck">Lübeck</a> law to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greifswald">Greifswald</a> in 1250. After he died childless in 1264, Barnim I ruled the whole duchy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wartislaw-iii-duke-of-pomerania.jpg" alt="Wartislaw III, Duke of Pomerania" width="320" height="244" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bonio · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eldena_tablica.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
